concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wc a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23WC How forensic procedures may be authorised in different"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-23wc ;
    values:originalText "circumstances  The following table shows the circumstances in which a forensic procedure may be carried out on a suspect, and shows the provisions that authorise the carrying out of the procedure.  Authority for forensic procedures  Suspect Intimate forensic procedure Non-intimate forensic procedure 1 adult not in custody with informed consent under Division 3 by order of a magistrate under" ;
    skos:definition "circumstances  The following table shows the circumstances in which a forensic procedure may be carried out on a suspect, and shows the provisions that authorise the carrying out of the procedure.  Authority for forensic procedures  Suspect Intimate forensic procedure Non-intimate forensic procedure 1 adult not in custody with informed consent under Division 3 by order of a magistrate under"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a8e7da6d25c27ba9e51207803e5448cc7652b4612469806b8a565f3c32035367" ;
    cof:pageNumber "29"^^xsd:integer ;
