concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wm-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23WM(3) Non-intimate forensic procedure may be carried out by"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-23wm-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) This Division does not authorise keeping a suspect in custody, in order to carry out a forensic procedure, after the expiration of the investigation period provided for by Part IC. Note: If it is necessary to keep a suspect in custody after the expiration of the Part IC investigation period in order to carry out a forensic procedure, an order of a magistrate under Division 5 will have to be obtained to authorise this." ;
    skos:definition "(3) This Division does not authorise keeping a suspect in custody, in order to carry out a forensic procedure, after the expiration of the investigation period provided for by Part IC. Note: If it is necessary to keep a suspect in custody after the expiration of the Part IC investigation period in order to carry out a forensic procedure, an order of a magistrate under Division 5 will have to be obtained to authorise this."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f37ba3521d10c34b20e6082f53a4fcd890454bffd9c6c086f7d869bbe915773c" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wm ;
    cof:pageNumber "44"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Keeping a suspect in custody after investigation period expiration requires magistrate order." ;
