concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wp a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23WP Record of senior police officer’s order"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-23wp ;
    values:originalText "(1) The senior police officer must, at the time of, or as soon as practicable after, make an order under section 23WN, make a record of:  (a) the order made; and  (b) the date and time when the order was made; and  (c) the reasons for making it; and must sign the record.  (2) The senior police officer must ensure that a copy of the record is made available to the suspect as soon as practicable after the record is made.   Forensic procedures  Part ID Forensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5  Section 23WQ  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The senior police officer must, at the time of, or as soon as practicable after, make an order under section 23WN, make a record of:  (a) the order made; and  (b) the date and time when the order was made; and  (c) the reasons for making it; and must sign the record.  (2) The senior police officer must ensure that a copy of the record is made available to the suspect as soon as practicable after the record is made.   Forensic procedures  Part ID Forensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5  Section 23WQ  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9c4781b3d213f40e256d9efa015be13f6ca26e92bbef116d1ce7ff9752ea3e7e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "46"^^xsd:integer ;
