    values:originalText "(1) An order may only be made in the presence of the suspect concerned, subject to any contrary order made by the magistrate." ;
    cof:pageNumber "51"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wy a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23WY Making of order"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-23wy ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a magistrate makes an order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure, the magistrate must:   Forensic procedures  Part ID Forensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5  Section 23XA  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (a) give reasons for making the order; and  (b) ensure that a written record of the order is kept; and  (c) order the suspect to attend for the carrying out of the forensic procedure; and  (d) inform the suspect that reasonable force may be used to ensure that he or she complies with the order for the carrying out of the forensic procedure.  (2) The magistrate may give directions as to the time, place and manner in which the procedure is to be carried out. Subdivision C—Interim orders" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If a magistrate makes an order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure, the magistrate must:   Forensic procedures  Part ID Forensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5  Section 23XA  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (a) give reasons for making the order; and  (b) ensure that a written record of the order is kept; and  (c) order the suspect to attend for the carrying out of the forensic procedure; and  (d) inform the suspect that reasonable force may be used to ensure that he or she complies with the order for the carrying out of the forensic procedure.  (2) The magistrate may give directions as to the time, place and manner in which the procedure is to be carried out. Subdivision C—Interim orders"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "48722e67ab5337f408aed2d98a9078e2f0f2950b597f02e1fdb8b7b95e9605f8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "52"^^xsd:integer ;
