concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xg a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23XG Results of forensic procedure carried out under interim order"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-23xg ;
    values:originalText "(1) A sample taken under an interim order must not be analysed unless:  (a) the sample is likely to perish before a final order is made; or  (b) a final order is made.  (2) A person who conducts an analysis in the circumstances set out in paragraph (1)(a) must not intentionally disclose the results of the analysis to any person:  (a) during the period before a final order is made; or  (b) if the interim order is disallowed. Penalty for a contravention of subsection (2): Imprisonment for 12 months." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A sample taken under an interim order must not be analysed unless:  (a) the sample is likely to perish before a final order is made; or  (b) a final order is made.  (2) A person who conducts an analysis in the circumstances set out in paragraph (1)(a) must not intentionally disclose the results of the analysis to any person:  (a) during the period before a final order is made; or  (b) if the interim order is disallowed. Penalty for a contravention of subsection (2): Imprisonment for 12 months."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9e772213462f28f37f337278b4f38e53c1880a28689e66d1420d45b319636b1f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "57"^^xsd:integer ;
