concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23ye a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23YE Powers etc. of legal representatives and interview friends"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-23ye ;
    values:originalText "(1) A request or objection that may be made by a suspect or offender under this Part may be made on the suspect’s or offender’s behalf by:  (a) in any case—the suspect’s or offender’s legal representative; or  (b) if the suspect or offender is a child or an incapable person— an interview friend of the suspect or offender; or  (c) if the investigating constable believes on reasonable grounds that the suspect or offender is an Aboriginal person or a Torres Strait Islander—an interview friend of the suspect or offender.  (2) If:  (a) a provision of this Part requires a suspect or offender to be informed of a matter; and  (b) an interview friend or legal representative of the suspect is present when the suspect or offender is to be so informed; and  (c) the suspect or offender is so informed in a language (including in sign language or braille) in which the suspect’s or offender’s interview friend or legal representative is not able to communicate with reasonable fluency; the interview friend or legal representative must also be informed of the matter in a language in which the interview friend or legal representative is able to communicate with reasonable fluency." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A request or objection that may be made by a suspect or offender under this Part may be made on the suspect’s or offender’s behalf by:  (a) in any case—the suspect’s or offender’s legal representative; or  (b) if the suspect or offender is a child or an incapable person— an interview friend of the suspect or offender; or  (c) if the investigating constable believes on reasonable grounds that the suspect or offender is an Aboriginal person or a Torres Strait Islander—an interview friend of the suspect or offender.  (2) If:  (a) a provision of this Part requires a suspect or offender to be informed of a matter; and  (b) an interview friend or legal representative of the suspect is present when the suspect or offender is to be so informed; and  (c) the suspect or offender is so informed in a language (including in sign language or braille) in which the suspect’s or offender’s interview friend or legal representative is not able to communicate with reasonable fluency; the interview friend or legal representative must also be informed of the matter in a language in which the interview friend or legal representative is able to communicate with reasonable fluency."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9c59c351f02163e91f8732624d2583b598ff61182d6c56777acca803882285e7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "116"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23ye-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23ye-ss-2 ;
