concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-31 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "31 Judicial proceeding and tribunal definitions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-31 ;
    values:originalText "In this Act: federal judicial proceeding means:  (a) a judicial proceeding in or before:  (i) a federal court; or  (ii) a court exercising federal jurisdiction; or  (iii) a court of a Territory; or  (b) a judicial proceeding before a body or person acting under a law of:  (i) the Commonwealth; or  (ii) a Territory. judicial proceeding means (other than in section 3L):  (a) a proceeding in or before a court; or  (b) a proceeding:  (i) before a body, or a person, acting under a law of the Commonwealth, of a State or of a Territory; and  (ii) in which evidence may be taken on oath. judicial tribunal means a body or person (other than a court) before whom a judicial proceeding is conducted.   Offences relating to the administration of justice  Part III Judges and magistrates  Division 2  Section 34  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "In this Act: federal judicial proceeding means:  (a) a judicial proceeding in or before:  (i) a federal court; or  (ii) a court exercising federal jurisdiction; or  (iii) a court of a Territory; or  (b) a judicial proceeding before a body or person acting under a law of:  (i) the Commonwealth; or  (ii) a Territory. judicial proceeding means (other than in section 3L):  (a) a proceeding in or before a court; or  (b) a proceeding:  (i) before a body, or a person, acting under a law of the Commonwealth, of a State or of a Territory; and  (ii) in which evidence may be taken on oath. judicial tribunal means a body or person (other than a court) before whom a judicial proceeding is conducted.   Offences relating to the administration of justice  Part III Judges and magistrates  Division 2  Section 34  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7146e142f9b4b2debc90e247080026fdbb49778dae051d203c2f25b7ea8d1669" ;
    cof:pageNumber "152"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines judicial proceeding and tribunal." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-act-1914.pdf> ;
