doc:sec-36a-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "36A(1) Intimidation of witnesses etc." ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) the first person:  (i) threatens, intimidates or restrains another person; or  (ii) uses violence to, or inflicts an injury on, another person; or  (iii) causes or procures violence, damage, loss or disadvantage to another person; or  (iv) causes or procures the punishment of another person; and  (b) the first person does so on account of the other person having appeared, or being about to appear, as a witness in a judicial proceeding; and  (c) the judicial proceeding is a federal judicial proceeding. Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years." ;
    cof:pageNumber "156"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-36a-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "36A(2) Intimidation of witnesses etc."@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-36a-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.   Offences relating to the administration of justice  Part III Evidence and witnesses  Division 3  Section 37  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the offence. Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.   Offences relating to the administration of justice  Part III Evidence and witnesses  Division 3  Section 37  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "afb00c33adfcff9fcb1eb23b85e8622833ed87805b46803ef01f82c831066f4f" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-36a ;
