doc:sec-37-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "37(1) Corruption of witnesses" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) the first person:  (i) gives, confers or procures any property, or benefit, of any kind to, upon or for another person; or  (ii) promises or offers to give, to confer, to procure or to attempt to procure any property, or benefit, of any kind to, upon or for another person; or  (iii) asks for, receives or obtains any property, or benefit, of any kind for himself or herself or another person; or  (iv) agrees to receive or to obtain any property, or benefit, of any kind for himself or herself or another person; and  (b) the first person does so upon an agreement or understanding that any person called, or to be called, as a witness in a judicial proceeding will:  (i) give false testimony; or  (ii) withhold true testimony; and  (c) the judicial proceeding is a federal judicial proceeding. Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years." ;
    cof:pageNumber "157"^^xsd:integer .

