    values:originalText "(3) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1) even if:  (a) charging a person falsely pursuant to the agreement is impossible; or  (b) the only other party to the agreement is a body corporate; or  (c) each other party to the agreement is a person who is not criminally responsible; or   Offences relating to the administration of justice  Part III Perverting the course of justice  Division 4  Section 42  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (d) subject to subsection (4), all other parties to the agreement have been acquitted of the offence." ;
    cof:pageNumber "160"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "41(4) Conspiracy to bring false accusation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-41-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) A person cannot be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1) if:  (a) all other parties to the agreement have been acquitted of such an offence; and  (b) a finding of guilt would be inconsistent with their acquittal." ;
    skos:definition "(4) A person cannot be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1) if:  (a) all other parties to the agreement have been acquitted of such an offence; and  (b) a finding of guilt would be inconsistent with their acquittal."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ddb15bd569ef1fe8a4a4a1ff1b06d3c5d2e358e023cefae65971ebf49b296e50" ;
