concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-44 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "44 Compounding offences"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-44 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) the first person:  (i) asks for, receives or obtains any property, or benefit, of any kind for himself or herself or another person; or  (ii) agrees to receive or to obtain any property, or benefit, of any kind for himself or herself or another person; and  (b) the first person does so upon an agreement or understanding that the first person will:  (i) compound or conceal an offence; or  (ii) abstain from, discontinue or delay a prosecution for an offence; or  (iii) withhold evidence of an offence; and" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) the first person:  (i) asks for, receives or obtains any property, or benefit, of any kind for himself or herself or another person; or  (ii) agrees to receive or to obtain any property, or benefit, of any kind for himself or herself or another person; and  (b) the first person does so upon an agreement or understanding that the first person will:  (i) compound or conceal an offence; or  (ii) abstain from, discontinue or delay a prosecution for an offence; or  (iii) withhold evidence of an offence; and"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "16ed3ed5bf97e8dd7467f422032a1234eaef004425370b9c9ad145b67df2216f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "163"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Agreement to compound or conceal an offence" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-act-1914.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.163" ;
