doc:sec-44 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "44 Compounding offences" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) the first person:  (i) asks for, receives or obtains any property, or benefit, of any kind for himself or herself or another person; or  (ii) agrees to receive or to obtain any property, or benefit, of any kind for himself or herself or another person; and  (b) the first person does so upon an agreement or understanding that the first person will:  (i) compound or conceal an offence; or  (ii) abstain from, discontinue or delay a prosecution for an offence; or  (iii) withhold evidence of an offence; and" ;
