doc:sec-45-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "45(1) Inserting advertisements without authority of court" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person inserts in the Gazette, or in a newspaper, an advertisement purporting to be published under the authority of a court; and  (b) the person does so:  (i) without authority; or  (ii) knowing the advertisement to be false in any material particular; and  (c) the advertisement purports to be published under the authority of:  (i) a federal court; or  (ii) a court exercising federal jurisdiction; or  (iii) a court of a Territory. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years." ;
    cof:pageNumber "164"^^xsd:integer .

