concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-56 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "56 Evidence of certain matters"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-56 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A certificate by the Foreign Affairs Minister, or by an eligible person authorised by that Minister to make such a certificate, stating that:  (a) specified waters were, at a specified time:  (i) part of the high seas; or  (ii) within the coastal sea of Australia; or  (b) a specified place was, at a specified time, a place beyond the jurisdiction of any country; is, for the purposes of any proceedings for an offence against this Part, evidence of the facts stated in the certificate.  (2) In this section: eligible person means an SES employee in the Foreign Affairs Department.   Offences relating to postal services  Part VIIA  Section 85E  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A certificate by the Foreign Affairs Minister, or by an eligible person authorised by that Minister to make such a certificate, stating that:  (a) specified waters were, at a specified time:  (i) part of the high seas; or  (ii) within the coastal sea of Australia; or  (b) a specified place was, at a specified time, a place beyond the jurisdiction of any country; is, for the purposes of any proceedings for an offence against this Part, evidence of the facts stated in the certificate.  (2) In this section: eligible person means an SES employee in the Foreign Affairs Department.   Offences relating to postal services  Part VIIA  Section 85E  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ebf2de9976bab38425cf3a887910f38fd41bd7639b1e0fc835032b2a72128d2b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "174"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-56-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-56-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-act-1914.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.174" .
