concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85f-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "85F(5) Interpretation—expressions used in Australian Postal"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-85f-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) A person shall not make, use, have in his or her possession, or sell or otherwise dispose of, any die, plate or instrument capable of making a mark, label or design in the form of, or in a form resembling, apparently intended to resemble or pass for, or likely to be mistaken for, a postage stamp, knowing that it is such a die, plate or instrument.   Offences relating to postal services  Part VIIA  Section 85H  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years." ;
    skos:definition "(5) A person shall not make, use, have in his or her possession, or sell or otherwise dispose of, any die, plate or instrument capable of making a mark, label or design in the form of, or in a form resembling, apparently intended to resemble or pass for, or likely to be mistaken for, a postage stamp, knowing that it is such a die, plate or instrument.   Offences relating to postal services  Part VIIA  Section 85H  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6f2a21135fc71cdec758f8c0f2db8fbee14e272cfd93b1bafeabe769baa4702d" ;
